<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diophantus (general)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2nd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diophantus, son of Asclepiodorus, was a general from Sinope in the service of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridates-vi-of-pontus">Mithridates VI of Pontus</a> in the late 2nd century BCE. Sent to help Chersonesus Taurica against the Crimean <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scythians">Scythians</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palakus">Palacus</a>, he won several campaigns in about 110–107 BCE and then crushed the revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saumacus">Saumacus</a> in the Bosporan Kingdom. A decree of Chersonesus honouring him is the main source for these events.</p></div>
